# Part Five — The Index of Thinkers

> About 115 thinkers, activists and authors you may cite, in alphabetical order, each with the key work and year and the one idea to remember. The **Topic** column shows where each is taught.

## 5.1  A to F

::: table | Thinkers A–F.
@widths 3.4,3.8,5.2,1.6
@font 9
Thinker | Key work (year) | Idea to remember | Topic
Abu-Lughod, Lila | "Do Muslim Women Really Need Saving?" (2002) | Critique of "saving" Muslim women as a pretext | T4
Agarwal, Bina | "The Gender and Environment Debate" (1992); *A Field of One's Own* (1994) | Feminist environmentalism; women's land rights | T2, T4
Aristotle | *Politics*; *Generation of Animals* | The female as an "incomplete" male — classic essentialism | T1
Auclert, Hubertine | (1882) | First to call herself a "feminist" | T2
Bandura, Albert | Bobo doll (1961); *Aggression: A Social Learning Analysis* (1973) | Violence and gender roles are learned by imitation | T1, T7
Barlas, Asma | *"Believing Women" in Islam* (2002) | Anti-patriarchal reading of the Qur'an | T2
Beauvoir, Simone de | *The Second Sex* (1949) | "One is not born, but rather becomes, a woman"; woman as "Other" | T1, T2
Bem, Sandra | Bem Sex-Role Inventory (1974); gender schema theory (1981) | Androgyny; mental schemas filter experience | T1
Benston, Margaret | "The Political Economy of Women's Liberation" (1969) | Housework as unpaid production | T2, T4
Berger, Peter and Luckmann, Thomas | *The Social Construction of Reality* (1966) | Reality is socially constructed | T1
Bhutto, Benazir | PM 1988–90, 1993–96 | First woman PM of a Muslim-majority country | T3, T6
Boserup, Ester | *Woman's Role in Economic Development* (1970) | Development bypassed or harmed women; origin of WID | T4
Brownmiller, Susan | *Against Our Will* (1975) | Rape as power that keeps women in fear | T7
Butler, Judith | *Gender Trouble* (1990) | Gender is performative — repeated acts create it | T1, T2
Chant, Sylvia and Sweetman, Caroline | (2012) | Critique of "smart economics" | T4
Chatterjee, Partha | "The Nationalist Resolution of the Women's Question" (1989) | Women as guardians of the "inner" spiritual world | T4
Chattopadhyay, Raghabendra and Duflo, Esther | (2004) | Women panchayat heads invested more in drinking water | T6
Childs, Sarah and Krook, Mona Lena | (2009) | Critical actors matter more than critical mass | T6
Chodorow, Nancy | *The Reproduction of Mothering* (1978) | Women's mothering reproduces gender | T1, T2
Cixous, Hélène | "The Laugh of the Medusa" (1975) | *Écriture féminine* | T2
Collins, Patricia Hill | *Black Feminist Thought* (1990) | Matrix of domination | T2, T5
Combahee River Collective | Statement (1977) | Interlocking oppressions; identity politics | T2
Connell, R. W. (Raewyn) | *Gender and Power* (1987); *Masculinities* (1995) | Hegemonic masculinity; patriarchal dividend | T1, T2, T7
Crenshaw, Kimberlé | (1989); "Mapping the Margins" (1991) | Intersectionality | T2, T5, T7
Dahlerup, Drude | (1988); *Women, Quotas and Politics* (2006) | Critical mass and critical acts; "fast track" vs "incremental track" | T6
Dalla Costa, Mariarosa and James, Selma | *The Power of Women and the Subversion of the Community* (1972) | Wages for housework | T2, T4
d'Eaubonne, Françoise | (1974) | Coined "ecofeminism" | T2, T4
Dobash, R. Emerson and Russell | *Violence Against Wives* (1979) | Wife-beating as male authority and entitlement | T7
Eagly, Alice and Carli, Linda | *Through the Labyrinth* (2007) | Women's path to leadership as a labyrinth | T6
Eisenstein, Zillah | (1979) | Capitalist patriarchy | T2
Elson, Diane | *Male Bias in the Development Process* (1991) | Adjustment treats women's labour as "infinitely elastic" | T4
Engels, Friedrich | *The Origin of the Family, Private Property and the State* (1884) | "World historical defeat of the female sex" | T2, T4
Escobar, Arturo | *Encountering Development* (1995) | Development as a discourse of power | T4
Fathalla, Mahmoud | Safe Motherhood Conference, Nairobi (1987) | "Why did Mrs X die?" — the road to maternal death | T5
Fausto-Sterling, Anne | "The Five Sexes" (1993); *Sexing the Body* (2000) | Sex as a spectrum | T1
Federici, Silvia | *Caliban and the Witch* (2004) | Witch-hunts and early capitalism | T4
Firestone, Shulamith | *The Dialectic of Sex* (1970) | Sex class; reproduction as the root of oppression | T2
Foucault, Michel | *The History of Sexuality*, vol. 1 (1976) | Sexuality and power produced by discourse | T1, T2
Frank, Andre Gunder | "The Development of Underdevelopment" (1966) | Dependency theory | T4
Friedan, Betty | *The Feminine Mystique* (1963) | "The problem that has no name"; co-founded NOW (1966) | T2, T3
:::

